      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_Washington",
      "category": "transport",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Riverside was officially incorporated on December 22, 1913.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Riverside%2C_Washington",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "After the railroad arrived in 1915, Riverside’s bustling steamboat trade faded, turning the town into a quiet ghost town.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        5,
        10
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://unitedstatesghosttowns.com/riverside-washington-ghost-town/",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The hilltop cemetery in Riverside contains the grave of outlaw Frank Watkins, a striking reminder of the town’s ghost‑town past.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        6,
        11
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
